commit 38db03756989a8c2cc3b203d35424081eba8df4a
Author: Alexey Sachkov <alexey.sachkov@intel.com>
Date:   Fri Apr 30 17:20:58 2021 +0300

    Relax handling of boolean specialization constants (#1015)
    
    When SPIR-V friendly IR is used, it might be the case that it was
    generated by some other LLVM tool and/or pass and for boolean types it
    is possible that they are represented as i8 instead of i1 in LLVM IR
    (depending on how they were used in the original source file).
    
    This patch adjusts and relaxes handling of boolean specialization
    constants from SPIR-V friendly IR to get the following signatures
    acceptable: `i1 _Z20__spirv_SpecConstantia(i32, i8)`.

