commit ee145be0b3f4b05b29beee8b1d18c26715437d14
Author: Artem Gindinson <artem.gindinson@intel.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 14:29:14 2020 +0300

    Translate the llvm.fshl intrinsic function
    
    "Funnel shift left" doesn't have an analogue in the OpenCL
    ExtInst set. We unroll `llvm.fshl.i<n>(i<n>, i<n>, i<n>)`
    into a small algorithm that performs the actual funnel shift.
    
    A detailed description of FSHL can be found at
    https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#llvm-fshl-intrinsic
    
    The generated SPIR-V implementation can be slightly optimized
    for scalar integers, but since llvm_fshl_* functions are replaced
    by the intrinsics in backwards translation, a slightly less optimal
    implementation is just a minor concern for non-LLVM-based
    backends.
    
    Signed-off-by: Artem Gindinson <artem.gindinson@intel.com>

