Author: Alexey Sotkin <alexey.sotkin@intel.com>
Date:   Mon May 25 13:27:06 2020 +0300

    Emit error if WordCount exceeds 16-bit max value
    
    According to the SPIR-V specification(Table 2) the 16 high-order bits of every
    instruction encode word count(length) of the instruction. This fundamental
    limitation doesn't allow to have instruction longer than 65535 words.
    
    Signed-off-by: Alexey Sotkin <alexey.sotkin@intel.com>

