commit 08ab82a585ee76b108c18c285c8e306795471837
Author: Artem Gindinson <artem.gindinson@intel.com>
Date:   Tue Dec 31 11:54:01 2019 +0300

    Enhance FPGA IVDep attribute testing
    
    The particular order of !"llvm.loop.parallel_access_indices" metadata
    operands being non-deterministic and irrelevant, it makes sense to
    alleviate the LIT tests from the corresponding restriction on the index
    groups' order.
    
    E.g. both of the below scenarios would now pass the tests:
    !0 = !{!"llvm.loop.parallel_access_indices", !1, !2}
    OR
    !0 = !{!"llvm.loop.parallel_access_indices", !2, !1}
    
    The tweaks of SPIRV types' checks fall into the same category.
    
    Signed-off-by: Artem Gindinson <artem.gindinson@intel.com>

