    Switch some .cl tests to use -fdeclare-opencl-builtins
    
    Clang's `-fdeclare-opencl-builtins` option now supports enough
    builtins that these tests can use the faster TableGen based builtin
    function declaration mechanism.  We still need the
    `-finclude-default-header` option for OpenCL specific types and
    constants, but when combined with `-fdeclare-opencl-builtins`, Clang
    will not parse the full header with OpenCL builtin declarations.
    
    This reduces the running time of the llvm-spirv test suite.

