commit ff618208913e8d08e9fd1f2760d39a7b6b0040c4
Author: Mikhail Lychkov <mikhail.lychkov@intel.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 4 14:56:58 2019 +0300

    [SYCL][FPGA] Skip *.annotation call debug info
    
    Currently there is no analogue of *.annotation intrinsic in SPIR-V.
    During IR translation this call is skipped or stored as a decoration.
    Position of this intrinsic in a basic block of IR after reverse
    translation may change or even lost. However, debug scope of the call
    may be translated into SPIR-V in inappropriate place and result in
    corruption of debug metadata for other instructions in that basic
    block. Even if debug info of the call doesn't corrupt debug info of
    other instructions in that basic block it isn't restored for the call
    during reverse translation.
    Skip debug scope info of *.annotation intrinsic call as it is useless
    for now.
    
    Signed-off-by: Mikhail Lychkov <mikhail.lychkov@intel.com>

