Author: Alexey Sachkov <alexey.sachkov@intel.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 7 17:35:12 2019 +0300

    Update extensions handling infrastucture
    
    This patch merges existing map of exention names with new one which is
    controllable by `--spirv-ext` command line option and enables usage of
    the new infrastructure for extensions in the translator.
    
    Now, before inserting any instruction, check for validity of such
    insertion must be performed: new method
    `SPIRV::SPIRVEntry::isAllowedToUseExtension` is added.
    
    If translator tries to generated a SPIRV entity which requires extension
    which wasn't enabled, assertion in `SPIRV::SPIRVValue::getRequiredExtensions`
    will fail. This assertion fires if and only if SPIRV entity is
    associated with any SPIR-V extension via `getRequriedExtensions` method.
    
    This patch introduces a bunch of LIT test failures because extension was
    used even if it was disabled.
    These failures will be fixed in the following commits.
    
    Signed-off-by: Alexey Sachkov <alexey.sachkov@intel.com>

