commit 28a5a61a8944ecee965aafa2183a9c239260a1fe
Author: Alexey Sotkin <alexey.sotkin@intel.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 2 15:19:22 2019 +0300

    Map memory semantics and memory order enums in runtime
    
    The "memory_order" and "memory_semantics" arguments of atomic OpenCL builtins
    are not always compile/translation time known constants. In this case can map
    OpenCL enums to SPIR-V enums in runtime.
    The same is applicable for translation from SPIR-V to LLVM IR. Scope<id> and
    MemorySemantics<id> operands are 32-bit integer scalars. They are guaranteed
    to be OpConstants only for Shader capabilites, not for Kernel.

commit b25f2019dc39892cdd01d83a4711f21aa1a30d86
Author: Sven van Haastregt <sven.vanhaastregt@arm.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 1 15:34:09 2019 +0100

    Gracefully fail on unimplemented opcodes
    
    Various SPIR-V opcodes have not been implemented in the translator
    yet, particularly shader-specific opcodes.  When reading a .spv or
    .spt file containing one of these unimplemented opcodes, the
    translator used to crash.
    
    Instead of crashing, emit an error when reading an unimplemented
    opcode.  To do so, introduce a new SPIRVEntryUnimplemented subclass
    and map all unimplemented opcodes to it.

