Date:   Thu May 23 08:31:50 2019 +0300

    Fix debug information interfering with loop controls translation
    
    According to the SPIR-V specification, branch merge instructions
    must immediately precede branch instructions. The patch ensures
    that ExtInst predecessors of branch instructions:
    
    - are inserted before the merge instructions;
    - and thus do not break SPIRVToLLVM translation of the latter.

commit cc04d1617ecde9ad739818bd3aaf84c0515042e6
Author: Dmitry Sidorov <dmitry.sidorov@intel.com>
Date:   Wed May 15 14:50:25 2019 +0300

    Support partial unrolling
    
    Possible use cases:
    
    unroll [N]
    going to be translated into:
    SPIR-V: 5 LoopMerge [X] [Y] 256 [N]
    LLVM-IR: !{!"llvm.loop.unroll.count", i32 [N]}
    
    unroll 1
    in this case loop unrolling should be disabled,
    going to be translated into:
    LLVM-IR: !{!"llvm.loop.unroll.disable"}
    
    unrolling behaviour without the hint was changed as well, see:
    LLVM-IR: !{!"llvm.loop.unroll.full"} -> !{!"llvm.loop.unroll.enable"}

