commit 62fe6db8d08e302a8776095871a602064956556f
Author: Stuart Brady <stuart.brady@arm.com>
Date:   Tue Apr 16 17:27:54 2019 +0100

    Add separate functions for reading and translating SPIR-V
    
    The OpenCL runtime API requires that IL be loaded and compiled with
    separate function calls:
    
     1. clCreateProgramWithIL(), which must check that the IL is well-formed
        and return CL_INVALID_VALUE if it is not.
    
     2. clBuildProgram() or clCompileProgram(), which allow build options to
        be specified.
    
    To facilitate the above, this change adds two new API functions:
    
     1. readSpirvModule(), which reads an istream to produce a SPIRVModule.
    
     2. convertSpirvToLLVM(), which converts a SPIRVModule to LLVM IR.
    
    The existing readSpirv() function is refactored in terms of these calls,
    but is kept in the API for the convenience of tools such as llvm-spirv.

commit 35666af57de67ee15e9074da7f42b8d628be965c
Author: Dmitry Sidorov <dmitry.sidorov@intel.com>
Date:   Mon May 6 14:52:28 2019 +0300

    Initial support of FPGA loop attributes/pragmas
    
    Following attributes/pragmas are supported:
     1. ivdep
     2. ivdep safelen(N)
     3. ii(N)
     4. max_concurrency_loop(N)
    
    LLVM IR->SPIRV translation (appropriately the set order):
     1. !"llvm.loop.ivdep.enable ->
        4 LoopMerge {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 4
     2. !"llvm.loop.ivdep.safelen", i32 N ->
        5 LoopMerge {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 8 N
     3. !"llvm.loop.ii.count", i32 N ->
        6 LoopMerge {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 0x80000000 5889 N
     4. !"llvm.loop.max_concurrency.count", i32 N ->
        6 LoopMerge {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 0x80000000 5890 N
    
    Also a case of multiple bit masks set for LoopControl is
    now supported.
    
    SPEC: KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Registry#28

