commit 665d001df8e4b2636fdca313c6b93658dca05799
Author: Sven van Haastregt <sven.vanhaastregt@arm.com>
Date:   Mon Jan 14 11:29:04 2019 +0000

    Align image type mangling to clang
    
    The mangling of OpenCL image types has been changed by clang commit
    aa8b893ccd ("[OpenCL] Complete image types support.", 2016-04-08), and
    until now the translator was emitting the old mangled names that did
    not include the access qualifier.
    
    Align with clang, to aid unifying subsequent compilation after
    importing SPIR-V into the LLVM domain.
    
    Image types with different access qualifiers in clang are separate
    types.  With this commit we also make them separate types in the
    translator, so for every image type there is a read_only, write_only,
    and read_write variant.  This keeps image type handling pretty much
    the same as handling of any other type in the translator.
    
    Updating tests was mostly done manually, as it is not trivial to
    select the correct access qualifier using just regexps.

