    Add tests for debug info support
    
    Testing of debug info feature in SPIR-V is based on idea that after round-trip
    translation of an LLVM module to SPIR-V and back debug info metadata should
    stay practically the same as before the translation and thus regular tests for
    DebugInfo in LLVM should pass.
    The tests being added with this commit are taken from llvm/test/DebugInfo
    directory. Translation to SPIR-V and back is added to every test. Also some
    minor modification required to make the tests translatable to SPIR-V are made.
    
    Building dependencies for debug info tests takes too long, so Travis CI
    terminates the build due to timeout. This commit introduces
    SKIP_SPIRV_DEBUG_INFO_TEST variable in cmake files. Set to true this variable
    disables tests in test/DebugInfo directory and excludes tools required for
    these tests from the build. By default the variable is not set, i.e. debug info
    tests for SPIR-V do run.

