commit 9f51c5cc91c5ab143f0fe9a69f39ffafbc43446b
Author: Andrew Savonichev <andrew.savonichev@intel.com>
Date:   Wed May 18 20:45:24 2016 +0300

    [SPIR-V] Fix translation of OpControlBarrier and OpMemoryBarrier (#134)
    
    * [SPIR-V] Fix translation of OpControlBarrier and OpMemoryBarrier
    
    Fixes: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-LLVM/issues/122
    
    OpControlBarrier and OpMemoryBarrier are now correctly translated to SPIR-V and
    vice versa.
    
    OpControlBarrier will be translated to:
      - barrier() if OpSource is OpenCL 1.2 and execution scope is Workgroup
      - work_group_barrier() if OpSource is OpenCL 2.0 or higher and the execution
        scope is Workgroup
      - sub_group_barrier() if execution scope is Subgroup
    
    OpMemoryBarrier will be translated to:
      - mem_fence() if OpSource is OpenCL 1.2
      - atomic_work_item_fence() if OpSource is OpenCL 2.0 or higher
    
    If OpSource is not specified, we assume it is the highest available version.
    
    * Use numeric values for mem scope and semantic

