commit ba2683b503290a1789f3a8eb874350bca9946191
Author: Andrey Lizunov <andrey.e.lizunov@intel.com>
Date:   Tue Feb 2 16:25:15 2016 +0300

    [SPIR 2.0] Add defines for address spaces of special OCL types
    
    SPIR 2.0 specification define address space for some of special
    opaque types it introduces as private. See the following note:
    "Note: By default, objects reside in the private address space
    (number 0). No address space qualification is used to indicate
    the private address space."
    However ATM different vendors treat the specification differently
    so to make their lifes easier this commit introduces few defines
    to mitigate this.
    
    SPIRV_OCL_SPECIAL_TYPES_DEFAULT_ADDR_SPACE  - default
    SPIRV_QUEUE_T_ADDR_SPACE                    - queue_t
    SPIRV_EVENT_T_ADDR_SPACE                    - event_t
    SPIRV_CLK_EVENT_T_ADDR_SPACE                - clk_event_t
    SPIRV_RESERVE_ID_T_ADDR_SPACE               - reserve_id_t
    SPIRV_PIPE_ADDR_SPACE                       - pipe qualifed types
    SPIRV_IMAGE_ADDR_SPACE                      - image types
    
    Values what could be used for the defines above
    SPIRAS_Private    - private addr. space (default)
    SPIRAS_Global     - global addr. space
    SPIRAS_Constant   - constant addr. space
    SPIRAS_Local      - local addr. space
    SPIRAS_Generic    - generic addr. space
    
    E.g. CMake style
    add_definitions(-DSPIRV_OCL_SPECIAL_TYPES_DEFAULT_ADDR_SPACE=SPIRAS_Global)
    add_definitions(-DSPIRV_RESERVE_ID_T_ADDR_SPACE=SPIRAS_Private)
    
    Notice what SPIRV_OCL_SPECIAL_TYPES_DEFAULT_ADDR_SPACE is used
    as a default addr. space for queue_t, event_t, clk_event_t, and reserve_id_t
    types only. SPIR 2.0 spec. if quite clear about pipe and image types which
    should reside in __global addr space.

