Author: Alexey Sotkin <alexey.sotkin@intel.com>
Date:   Wed Dec 2 18:34:32 2015 +0300

    Linkage type mapping between LLVM and SPIRV is as follows:
    llvm private/internal linkage -> SPIRV Internal -> llvm internal linkage
    llvm global value definitions with available_externally linkage or with common linkage -> SPIRV Import -> llvm available_externally linkage
    llvm global value declaration(w/o available_externally or common linkage ) -> SPIRV Import -> llvm external linkage
    other llvm global values  -> SPIRV Export -> llvm external linkage

commit 23ef04bdf7481d8e09e80802d0c48e540c638a8c
Author: Alexey Sotkin <alexey.sotkin@intel.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 20 12:45:47 2015 +0300

    Changing linkage type mapping.
    Since global variables and functions with external linkage in C code
    can be mapped to either import or export linkage type in SPIR-V,
    new approach has been implemented:
    - global variables and function declarations are to be decorated with Import
     linkage type in SPIR-V.
    - global variables and function definitions are to be decorated with Export
     linkage type in SPIR-V.
    - variables and functions with internal linkage type will have default linkage
     type in SPIR-V, i.e. internal.
    
    Conflicts:
            lib/SPIRV/SPIRVWriter.cpp

