    Merge branch 'khronos/spirv-memory-access-encoding' into 'khronos/spirv-3.6.1'
    
    Khronos/spirv memory access encoding
    
    This patch fixes encoding of memory access literal.
    
    According to SPIR-V specification
    0x0 None
    0x1 Volatile - This access cannot be optimized away; it has to be executed.
    0x2 Aligned - This access has a known alignment, provided as a literal in the next operand.
    
    But it was
    0x0 Volatile - This access cannot be optimized away; it has to be executed.
    0x1 Aligned - This access has a known alignment, provided as a literal in the next operand.
    
    It's really hard to detect issues like this with the existing validation approach - use the same header for SPIR-V generator and consumer.
    
    See merge request !11

